{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7ebef90aebdae1aaf8c05e04d628fe0abe61bbbe14064247bca1bcda0b4ab6ef","digest":{"component_or_area":"tracker-footprint command","key_entities":["footprint.py","_pack_layer","measure_tracker","tracker_footprint.py","_render_text","DEFINITIONS[\"pack\"]","pack_layer schema","tests/unit/commands/test_tracker_footprint.py","docs/user-guide.md","docs/reuse-surface.md","git clone --shared","alternates","shared_reasons","complete boolean","st_blocks"],"problem_keywords":["shared clone","git alternates","pack layer","footprint measurement","edge case coverage","schema validation"],"propositions":["The mounted pack layer in alternates-backed shared clones reports near-zero size because it measures only the primary object database, not borrowed alternate objects, risking misinterpretation as a complete whole-object-store measurement.","Pack layer allocation measurement assumes a fixed filesystem block-to-byte ratio that fails on block-suballocating filesystems; it must use injected or stat-based block counts instead.","The text rendering path for allocation-unavailable state lacks direct unit test coverage.","The CLI bad-argument (argparse exit-2) path lacks direct unit test coverage.","The pack layer must carry an explicit `complete` boolean field—true for standalone and linked-worktree packs, false when alternates are present—so non-exclusive shared measurements are unambiguous."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787907364485063001,"uuid":"b8f5414c-363e-43df-a8d9-d1ee5536f2ff"}